     (I suppose you've already hit the page break, but whatever.)
     Anyway.  The uses I've found (seems to be all) are:
1. It will cure blindness, confusion, hallucination, or stunning when
   a)pplied, without running out.  Invaluble!
2. It will clear up a potion of sickness, hallucination, and I believe
   confusion when D)ipped in it, and not damage others.  Good test for
   bad potions.  Interestingly, water manufactured this way doesn't seem
   to mix with water manufactured by diluting other potions, so it's probably
   better when you're making holy water to dip such potions in fountains.
   (It's still a good test.)
3. Won't rust.  You can also enchant them.  Make great weapons against
   rust monsters, green jellies, acid blobs, and all of them creatures.
     So... a)pply, d)ip, w)ield.

     (Actually, a)pply, #d)ip, w)ield, to be technical.)
     By the way, 3 cursed scrolls of genocide make for a great way to gain
levels using wraiths, but for lower-level players, I find one of the single-
most valuble objects (at about char level 10-12) is a spellbook of create
monster.  Just keep creating wraiths until the spell runs out.  #HARD option
makes that to be about 4 levels worth of corpses, near as I can tell.  About
1/3 of wraiths seem to leave corpses in my experience.
     (Make sure your AC is enough so that they won't actually DRAIN levels...)
