     (Phew.  Line noise!)
     I, while I'm being prolific, experimented with the scrolls while confused.
I have a list of effects I was able to figure out:
enchant armor/enchant weapon: rustproof, of course
destroy armor: armor glows purple.  Little apparent effect.
Confuse monster: hands glow purple.  Again no effect.
Scare monster: "you hear a sad wailing in the distance." ???
create monster: prompts for ten different monsters; I suppose you could
   gain a lot of levels this way by entering "wraith" ten times.
taming: works anyway
genocide: fatal... you genocide your character class and die.
light: darkens room (as per cursed scroll)
teleportation: level teleport, 'course
gold detection: detects traps (!)
food detection: seems to work anyway
identify: "You identify the scroll as an identify scroll." (I figured as much.)
magic mapping: as per cursed scroll (bad map)
amnesia: partial amnesia; level looks like a cursed mag. mapping scroll's map
fire: scroll catches fire, 2-3hp temporary damage.
punishment: "You feel guilty", no effect
charging: "You feel charged up!", no effect
     If you've already found a scroll of genocide, this looks like a pretty
good way to identify some harmful scrolls, especially considering that the
enchant scrolls will benefit you anyway.  (identify scrolls seem to be the
greatest loss, but it still doesn't hurt you.)  It does require a potion of
confusion, though.  But, the scrolls of punishment, destroy monster, and
amnesia are all mitigated, along with fire.
     (I might add teleport to genocide as far as scrolls one would NOT want
to read while confused except at high levels or with a ring of teleport con-
trol.)
